/**
 * The foundation library's icons (Technical Product Marketing, V1.2): one for
 * each named document, all twelve from one professional outline family,
 * Phosphor Icons (https://phosphoricons.com), Regular weight, drawn on its own
 * 256-unit grid, so every card shares one line weight, optical size, padding
 * and curve language. Each card shows its icon large and faded, in the
 * document's accent, in one zone (TpmFlow.astro); the icon is decorative,
 * since the card's number, title and subline carry the meaning.
 *
 *   00 chats-circle     Stakeholder Interviews        Chats Circle: two speech bubbles
 *   01 stack            Strategic Foundation Brief    Stack: layered structure
 *   02 user-focus       Target Buyer Analysis         User Focus: one person framed by focus marks
 *   03 warning-diamond  Market Pain Points Research   Warning Diamond: a warning signal
 *   04 brain            Target Audience Psychology    Brain
 *   05 binoculars       Competitor Analysis           Binoculars
 *   06 crosshair        Product Positioning           Crosshair
 *   07 fingerprint      Brand Archetype               Fingerprint: a whorl with a clear center
 *   08 seal-check       Claims Log                    Seal Check: a verified seal
 *   09 tree-structure   Messaging Hierarchy           Tree Structure
 *   10 waveform         Brand Tone of Voice           Waveform
 *   11 book-open-text   Brand Lexicon                 Book Open Text: an open book with text
 *
 * Phosphor has no magnifying glass with a warning signal, the brief's first
 * direction for 03, so its warning signal alone stands for the pain points.
